      "value": "@{5f7d549362370d3eddd862f7|full_name}: the main issues with that approach are 1) complexity 2) the risk of ownership getting out of sync between those two objects and 3) additional bandwidth usage due to the overhead of having an additional object (this can to either way depending on the circumstances)\n\nYou’re right it can be worked around but it would be nice to avoid the complexities that workaround introduces.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
